    {
      "dependency_id": "RED-0001",
      "note": "Used only as a fixed seven-element list of (g,n) pairs, not as a cohomological hypothesis. The content asserted by the attempt, (3,12),(5,8),(6,6),(7,4),(8,0),(8,1),(8,2), matches the packet's own enumeration at FND-0035 verbatim. No Tate, weight, purity or motivic content of RED-0001 is invoked anywhere in the argument, so the 'predicted motive used as unconditional theorem' and 'pure Tate upgraded to algebraic generation' attacks have no surface.",
