{
  "attempt_id": "ATT-0142",
  "campaign_id": "C66BAR-001",
  "campaign_revision": 2,
  "checked_claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0138-1",
      "note": "Poincare duality for the smooth separated DM stack M_{5,8} of dimension d=3*5-3+8=20 identifies H^{BM}_{16} with H^{24}(20). Lowest weight on the ordinary side is W_{24}H^{24}, so W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{5,8};Q)=W_{24}H^{24}(M_{5,8};Q)(20). This is FND-0001 specialized at (5,8), matching the task target (open_bm_degree 16, ordinary_cohomology_degree 24, poincare_twist 20). Stack-level rational Betti/MHS only; no coarse-space or integral identification.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0138-2",
      "note": "vcd(M_{5,8})=4*5-4+8=24 equals the ordinary degree k=24, and n-1=7 equals the published inclusive endpoint c(5)=7. FND-0195 is stated for g>=2, n>=1, k=vcd, Tate_range n-1<=c(g) with c(5)=7, and excludes only degree vcd-1 of the target and unpublished c(8). The target degree is vcd, not vcd-1. Independently: SRC-0002 Table 1 and Proposition 4.5, THM-0005 (open M, all pure-weight pieces, n<=c(g)), and SRC-0004 Lemma 10.13 ('If n<=7, then M_{5,n} has the CKgP and A^*=R^*') all include n=7.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0138-3",
      "note": "FND-0195 already concludes that whenever n-1<=c(g) at k=vcd, W_{vcd}H^{vcd}(M_{g,n};Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-vcd/2). Substituting (5,8,24) gives W_{24}H^{24}(M_{5,8};Q)=Q(-12)^{oplus r}. The internal peel reconstruction matches the finding: Phi_{5,8}^{24}=0 because vcd(M_{5,7})=23 and H^{24}(M_{5,7};Q)=0 (strictly above vcd, not the blocked inference at 24=vcd(M_{5,8})); every Kunneth multi-index of C^8->M_5 with |i|<=8 has base degree >=16>vcd(M_5)=15, so the primitive quotient and every no-slot-2 summand vanish; survivors have some i_s=2 and are carried into Psi by FND-0196 (Morita disposal (1) gives b_s=0 for g>=2, and the PTY projector/induction disposals are likewise g-independent); FND-0197 supplies the restriction surjection W_{24}H^{24}(C^8)->W_{24}H^{24}(M_{5,8}) without using the mixed R^1 of the punctured forgetful map. Hodge type enters only through W_{22}H^{22}(M_{5,7};Q): Proposition 4.5 at n=7=c(5) gives algebraicity of every W_k H^k, hence type Q(-11) in even degree 22, and cup with psi of type Q(-1) yields a subquotient of Q(-12). Semisimplicity of polarizable pure weight-24 Hodge structures (inside FND-0195, and the same principle as FND-0033) upgrades that to an honest direct sum. Degree 22=vcd(M_{5,7})-1 is irrelevant: the FND-0195 exclusion of 'degree vcd-1' is about applying the peel at the target, while CKgP/Prop 4.5 has no degree restriction and FND-0195 itself types the source W_{vcd-2}H^{vcd-2}(M_{g,n-1}).",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
