1	{"id":"CONJ-0001","kind":"conjecture","title":"Degree-16 pure Tate target","statement":"For every stable pair (g,n), H^16(Mbar_g,n;Q) is a direct sum of Q(-8).","scope":{"degree":16,"g":"all","n":"all","object":"Mbar","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0001"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0001","locator":"Section 4, paragraph discussing even degrees 16,18,20","evidence_note":"The 2026 survey records degree 16 as predicted but open."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"cross_checked","truth_status":"conjectural","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Canonical mathematical target; see data/target.json."}
2	{"id":"THM-0001","kind":"theorem","title":"Smooth proper stack cohomology is pure","statement":"H^k of a smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack over C carries a pure Hodge structure of weight k.","scope":{"degree":"all","object":"smooth proper DM stack","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0001"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0001","locator":"Section 2.1","evidence_note":"The survey states the pure Hodge structure convention for smooth proper stacks."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"source_verified","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Shows that only the Tate-type condition is nontrivial."}
3	{"id":"THM-0002","kind":"theorem","title":"Low even degree cohomology is Tate through degree 14","statement":"For all stable (g,n), H^k(Mbar_g,n;Q) is a direct sum of Q(-k/2) for even k<=14.","scope":{"degree":"even <=14","g":"all","n":"all","object":"Mbar","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0002","SRC-0003"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Theorem 1.5(3) and discussion immediately after it","evidence_note":"Low even homology is tautological and duality gives the Hodge structures."},{"source_id":"SRC-0003","locator":"Theorem 1.2","evidence_note":"Earlier pure Hodge-Tate result through degree 12."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"cross_checked","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Degree-14 replay target."}
4	{"id":"THM-0003","kind":"theorem","title":"Boundary exact sequence reduces compactified cohomology to the open pure-weight quotient","statement":"The boundary long exact sequence yields a right-exact reduction from boundary homology to H_k(Mbar_g,n), with quotient W_{-k}H_k^BM(M_g,n).","scope":{"degree":"all","g":"all","n":"all","object":"Mbar boundary and open M","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0002"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Equation (6.1), page 24","evidence_note":"This is the exact sequence used for the low-homology induction."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"source_verified","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"A proof packet must track homology/cohomology duality and Tate twists explicitly."}
5	{"id":"THM-0004","kind":"theorem","title":"Finite base-case inequalities for low homology","statement":"In the low-homology induction at degree k, only n=0,1 with k>=2g or n>=2 with k>=2g-2+n require open-stratum base cases.","scope":{"degree":"fixed k","g":"finite range","n":"finite range","object":"open M","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0002"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Proof of Theorem 1.5(3), page 24","evidence_note":"The proof states the vanishing ranges and the complementary finite cases."}],"depends_on":["THM-0003"],"verification_status":"cross_checked","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Mechanically enumerated by pure_tate.cases."}
6	{"id":"THM-0005","kind":"theorem","title":"Published CKgP marking bounds through genus 7","statement":"M_g,n has CKgP and tautological Chow ring for n<=c(g), where c(3)=11,c(4)=11,c(5)=7,c(6)=5,c(7)=3; genus 0 is unrestricted.","scope":{"degree":"all pure-weight pieces","g":"0 through 7","n":"bounded by c(g)","object":"open M","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0002","SRC-0004"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Table 1 on page 12 and Proposition 4.5","evidence_note":"Records c(g) and derives algebraicity of the pure-weight cohomology."},{"source_id":"SRC-0004","locator":"Theorem 1.4 and CKgP results","evidence_note":"Primary source for most low-genus CKgP ranges."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"cross_checked","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"The degree-16 boundary of these ranges produces four pointed exceptional cases and genus 8."}
7	{"id":"THM-0006","kind":"theorem","title":"All even cohomology in genus 1 is tautological","statement":"For every n, the even cohomology of Mbar_1,n is represented by tautological boundary classes.","scope":{"degree":"even","g":1,"n":"all","object":"Mbar","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0002"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Proposition 2.4 discussion and proof of Theorem 1.5(3)","evidence_note":"The genus-one even case is discharged separately in the induction."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"source_verified","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Upstream primary references must be added during full corpus expansion."}
8	{"id":"THM-0007","kind":"theorem","title":"Genus-2 even cohomology through degree 20 is tautological","statement":"For k<=10 and all n, H^{2k}(Mbar_2,n) equals its tautological subspace.","scope":{"degree":"even <=20","g":2,"n":"all","object":"Mbar","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0002"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Corollary 2.7","evidence_note":"The paper states the genus-two result for every marking number."}],"depends_on":[],"verification_status":"source_verified","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Sufficient for the degree-16 reduction."}
9	{"id":"OBS-0001","kind":"observation","title":"Degree 16 remains open as of May 2026","statement":"The universal pure-Tate statement is known through even degree 14, while degrees 16,18,20 remain open.","scope":{"degree":[16,18,20],"g":"all","n":"all","object":"Mbar","coefficients":"Q"},"source_ids":["SRC-0001","SRC-0002"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0001","locator":"Section 4, current-status discussion","evidence_note":"Current survey explicitly records the open degrees."},{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Introduction after Theorem 1.5","evidence_note":"The 2024 paper presents these degrees as predictions."}],"depends_on":["THM-0002"],"verification_status":"cross_checked","truth_status":"established","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-29","notes":"Prevents spending effort reproving a later theorem without first finding it."}
10	{"id":"RED-0001","kind":"reduction","title":"Candidate finite obstruction for degree 16","statement":"Extending the published low-homology induction to degree 16 reduces the unresolved open input to W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}), expected Tate type Q(8), for (g,n)=(3,12),(5,8),(6,6),(7,4),(8,0),(8,1),(8,2). If d=3g-3+n, Poincare duality realizes this as W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n})(d); the untwisted ordinary group has Tate type Q(-(d-8)) and Chow codimension d-8.","scope":{"degree":16,"g":[3,5,6,7,8],"n":"listed cases","object":"open M Borel-Moore pure-weight piece and ordinary-cohomology dual","coefficients":"Q","context_revision":2},"source_ids":["SRC-0001","SRC-0002","SRC-0004"],"locators":[{"source_id":"SRC-0002","locator":"Equation (6.1), proof of Theorem 1.5(3), Table 1, Proposition 4.5","evidence_note":"The inequalities and coverage table are combined mechanically; duality conventions require the dimension-dependent ordinary degree."},{"source_id":"SRC-0001","locator":"Current-status discussion for degree 16","evidence_note":"Confirms that the global degree remains open."},{"source_id":"SRC-0004","locator":"Theorem 1.4 and the CKgP results used in the 2024 extension paper","evidence_note":"Supplies the published low-genus coverage behind most entries of the CKgP table."}],"depends_on":["CONJ-0001","THM-0002","THM-0003","THM-0004","THM-0005","THM-0006","THM-0007","OBS-0001"],"verification_status":"cross_checked","truth_status":"inferred","conditional":false,"confidence":"high","updated_on":"2026-07-30","notes":"Context revision v2 corrects the open-input duality while preserving the cross-checked seven-pair enumeration and audit provenance from RAUD-0001 (claude) and RAUD-0002 (grok)."}
